# Files that a macOS or Linux shell sources or executes must keep LF endings.
# `eas build` uploads the working tree as-is, so a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true was shipping ios/.xcode.env with CRLF. Xcode's build
# phases source that file, bash reads the bare CR on its blank line as a
# command, and "[Expo] Configure project" fails the archive.
*.sh text eol=lf
ios/.xcode.env text eol=lf
ios/.xcode.env.local text eol=lf
android/gradlew text eol=lf
